{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Qh7WrGhb84gNSy5EHQMxhq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to define three tiers (best/median/worst) for a Dream simulation based on their IRT person-fit contamination detection research. Let me carefully analyze the project context to define meaningful tiers.\n\nKey information from the context:\n\n1. **Current MVP results**:\n   - Phase A simulation: MMLU power@15% = 97.9%, HellaSwag 73.3%, GSM8K 57.8%, ARC-C 12.9%, HumanEval 24.3%\n   - Only MMLU passes 80% power threshold at 15% contamination\n   - The inverted-U pattern holds consistently across all benchmarks, and Phase B with Gemini-1.5 shows strong MMLU detection (lz*=+34.75) with signals replicating across other tasks\n\n2. **Core claims**:\n   - Claim 1: Minimal-information detection (binary only)\n   - Claim 2: Power is predictable function of n_items and contamination level, two signal regimes\n   - Claim 3: Empirical prevalence findings\n\n3. **Key experiments planned**:\n   - exp-ctrl-contam (ground truth): The most critical - controlled contamination on Qwen3.5-9B and Gemma-4-31B\n   - exp-leaderboard-audit: Large-scale scan\n   - exp-post-rl: Post-RL detection\n   - exp-power-theory: Theoretical derivation\n\n4. **Key risks**:\n   - No ground truth (biggest reviewer concern)\n   - Only 12 models + 5 benchmarks (scope)\n   - SFT generalization might smooth the signal\n   - Post-RL might destroy signal\n   - Small benchmarks have low power\n\nNow I'm mapping out the outcome scenarios. In the best case, the controlled contamination experiment produces clean lz* signals across all contamination levels, the power theory fits simulation data well, the leaderboard audit uncovers interesting patterns, and the two-sided framework cleanly separates partial from full contamination. In a median scenario, the controlled experiment works but with noisier signals that only emerge above certain thresholds, and SFT generalization partially smooths the domain-level leakage signal.\n\nIn the worst case, SFT generalization significantly dampens the lz* signal, detection only works for near-verbatim contamination rather than realistic partial cases, and post-RL completely destroys the signal, making the method only useful for extreme scenarios.\n\nI need to define specific metrics to track: AUROC of lz* for detecting contaminated versus clean models, effect size between them, minimum detectable contamination level at 80% power, and how well the power theory derivation matches the simulation results.\n\nI'm also tracking the power retention ratio after post-RL, the number of flagged models from the leaderboard audit, and AUROC advantage over existing baselines like ConStat and Min-K%++.\n\nFor the controlled contamination experiment, I'm setting performance thresholds: best case would be AUROC ≥ 0.95 at 15% contamination with detection starting at 5%, median case around 0.80-0.95 with detection at 15-25%, and worst case below 0.80 only detectable at 50%+.\n\nFor post-RL, I'm expecting best case power retention above 80%, median between 40-80%, and worst case below 40%.\n\nWriting the YAML configuration...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9836,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9836},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c14acc35-e720-45e2-8dc2-a986c6e07456","uuid":"22cfdd52-06a1-4bd5-aafc-c9a08683b6e4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Qh7WrGhb84gNSy5EHQMxhq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"控制实验完整验证核心假设：SFT 污染产生可检测的 lz* 信号，且信号在 post-RL 后大部分保留。原始 framing 全部成立。\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"SFT 污染在 binary response 层面产生足够强的 person-misfit 信号，不被泛化效应平滑\"\n      - \"双侧框架在控制实验中被验证——部分污染 lz*<<0，高污染 lz*>>0，拐点位置可预测\"\n      - \"Post-RL (GRPO) 后 lz* 信号大部分保留，Wang et al. (2025) 的 MIA 失效问题不适用于 person-fit\"\n      - \"Leaderboard audit 数据可获取，大规模扫描发现有意义的污染分布模式\"\n      - \"Power 理论推导与模拟数据高度吻合\"\n    number_ranges:\n      ctrl_contam_auroc_at_15pct: [0.93, 0.99]\n      ctrl_contam_min_detectable_level: [0.03, 0.08]\n      ctrl_contam_lz_effect_size_cohens_d: [1.5, 3.0]\n      post_rl_power_retention_ratio: [0.75, 0.95]\n      power_theory_r_squared: [0.95, 0.99]\n      leaderboard_models_scanned: [500, 7000]\n      leaderboard_flagged_rate: [0.05, 0.20]\n      baseline_auroc_advantage_vs_constat: [0.05, 0.15]\n      two_sided_inverted_u_inflection_contam_level: [0.55, 0.75]\n      mmlu_power_at_5pct_contam: [0.60, 0.85]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始 framing 完全成立。三条 claim 均有 ground-truth 支撑：(1) minimal-information operating point\n      经控制实验确认——仅 binary 数据即可在 5% 污染水平检测，AUROC>0.93；(2) power ∝ n_items 有解析公式，\n      inverted-U 从经验观察升级为理论命题，拐点位置可预测；(3) Gemini-1.5 case study + leaderboard audit\n      构成大规模实证贡献。Post-RL 实验直接回应 Wang et al.，形成\"MIA 失效但 person-fit 存活\"的对比叙事。\n      Headline: \"IRT-FIT 是唯一在 minimal-information 条件下同时解决 partial/full/post-RL 污染的方法\"。\n      EMNLP 主会议无需调整 claim 强度。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"控制实验验证核心信号存在但存在局限：SFT 泛化部分平滑信号（仅高污染或特定 domain 可检测），post-RL 显著衰减信号。需收窄 claims 范围。\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"SFT 污染信号存在，但泛化效应使低污染（<15%）区间信噪比不足，仅中高污染可靠检测\"\n      - \"双侧框架在数据上可观察但拐点不够 sharp——存在过渡区而非 clean separation\"\n      - \"Post-RL 后信号显著衰减（retention 40-75%），对部分模型 lz* 回到不显著区\"\n      - \"Leaderboard audit 数据仅部分可获取（~100-500 模型），或需要自己跑推理（GPU 预算紧张）\"\n      - \"Power 理论推导 R² 中等——公式描述趋势但非精确预测\"\n    number_ranges:\n      ctrl_contam_auroc_at_15pct: [0.78, 0.92]\n      ctrl_contam_min_detectable_level: [0.12, 0.25]\n      ctrl_contam_lz_effect_size_cohens_d: [0.8, 1.5]\n      post_rl_power_retention_ratio: [0.35, 0.74]\n      power_theory_r_squared: [0.80, 0.94]\n      leaderboard_models_scanned: [80, 500]\n      leaderboard_flagged_rate: [0.02, 0.10]\n      baseline_auroc_advantage_vs_constat: [-0.05, 0.08]\n      two_sided_inverted_u_inflection_contam_level: [0.40, 0.70]\n      mmlu_power_at_5pct_contam: [0.20, 0.55]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      需要调整 claim 强度和 scope。(1) Claim 1 从\"detect contamination\"收窄为\"detect moderate-to-heavy\n      SFT contamination (≥15%)\"——仍成立因为这是实际 leaderboard gaming 的典型水平；(2) Claim 2 保留\n      power ∝ n_items 但 inverted-U 描述为\"empirical characterization with approximate theoretical\n      backing\"而非精确理论；(3) Claim 3 保留 Gemini-1.5 case 但 leaderboard audit 从\"7K+ models\"\n      降为\"representative sample\"。Post-RL 结果诚实报告衰减并分析原因（reward hacking smoothing），\n      作为 limitation + future work。新增\"域级分析\"作为补偿贡献——展示污染集中在特定 MMLU domains。\n      Headline 调整为：\"IRT-FIT 在 minimal-information 条件下可靠检测中度以上 SFT 污染，\n      且在大型 benchmark 上 power>80%\"。EMNLP 仍可投但需增加 exp-domain-analysis 和更细致的 scope 声明。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"SFT 泛化严重平滑信号——控制实验显示 lz* 仅在近乎全量污染或完全 verbatim 记忆时才可检测。核心假设（binary 数据足以检测现实水平污染）不成立，需 reframe。\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"SFT 泛化使 partial contamination（5-25%）在 binary response 层面几乎不可区分于能力提升\"\n      - \"lz* 仅在极端情况下显著：>50% verbatim 污染或 Gemini-1.5 式 100% 全量泄漏\"\n      - \"Post-RL 完全破坏 person-fit 信号——RL 的 reward shaping 重塑 response pattern\"\n      - \"Leaderboard per-item logs 不可获取，自跑推理 GPU 预算不足以覆盖有意义规模\"\n      - \"Power 理论推导发现 4PL 的 d 参数引入不可忽略的 bias，lz* 理论保证在 4PL 下部分失效\"\n    number_ranges:\n      ctrl_contam_auroc_at_15pct: [0.55, 0.77]\n      ctrl_contam_min_detectable_level: [0.30, 0.60]\n      ctrl_contam_lz_effect_size_cohens_d: [0.2, 0.8]\n      post_rl_power_retention_ratio: [0.05, 0.34]\n      power_theory_r_squared: [0.50, 0.79]\n      leaderboard_models_scanned: [12, 80]\n      leaderboard_flagged_rate: [0.00, 0.03]\n      baseline_auroc_advantage_vs_constat: [-0.15, -0.02]\n      two_sided_inverted_u_inflection_contam_level: [0.25, 0.50]\n      mmlu_power_at_5pct_contam: [0.05, 0.20]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      核心假设不成立——binary response 的信息量不足以检测现实水平的 SFT 污染。必须 reframe，但不降级 venue。\n      新 angle：\"IRT person-fit 作为 benchmark integrity 的必要条件检查（necessary but not sufficient）\"。\n      Reframe 逻辑：(1) 将 lz* 定位为\"极端污染的高置信度筛选器\"而非通用检测器——Gemini-1.5 的 lz*=+34.75\n      仍是强结果，说明极端 case 的检出是 zero-cost（无需 access）的；(2) 将控制实验的\"负面结果\"本身作为贡献——\n      \"我们严格量化了 binary response 检测的信息论下界，证明 SFT 泛化是 binary-only 检测的根本瓶颈\"；\n      (3) 用 information-theoretic framing 构建 detection frontier 的完整图景——我们的负面结果 + 文献\n      正面结果共同刻画了\"信息量 vs 检测力\"的 Pareto 前沿。(4) 发展\"多统计量融合\"方向——lz* + outfit + infit\n      的联合检验是否能突破单统计量的信息瓶颈。Headline 变为：\"Binary response 检测的信息论极限：\n      IRT person-fit 何时足够、何时不够\"。EMNLP 仍可投——负面结果 + 理论分析 + frontier 框架\n      对评估方法论社区同样有价值。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9836,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9836},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c14acc35-e720-45e2-8dc2-a986c6e07456","uuid":"b14e2e53-042d-41c2-b693-dc8427602699"}
